{
  "_doc": [
    "The three shell themes. settings.json picks one with {\"theme\": {\"mode\": \"dark\" | \"light\" | \"glass\"}}.",
    "Every Theme.qml looks a key up here for the active mode and falls back to its own dark literal,",
    "which is why 'dark' is empty: dark IS the literals, so it cannot drift from what shipped.",
    "Glass draws the panels nearly clear; the frosting and refraction behind them come from the",
    "hyprglass Hyprland plugin (see hypr/glass.lua). Without the plugin, glass mode is just a",
    "very translucent dark theme.",
    "User overrides from the settings app win over this file: palette (dark), paletteLight, paletteGlass."
